{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261114T175120Z-01cf24db", "ts": "2026-11-14T17:54:31Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev.1", "branch": "feature/ci-testament", "build": "a4fbec6a030c"}, "body": {"base_commit": "01a39996ee079aab36941cf48acff20d1c32d56b", "base_tree": "2ebabf2045481285e38fe842f8d2f9498fbdcbae", "head_tree": "d1bfe1763ec4e84276502ef53808702aa12bebbf", "head_commit": "a4fbec6a030c18022fbbd47be91a6724df1ecda5", "dispatch_commit": "a4fbec6a030c18022fbbd47be91a6724df1ecda5", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", "documentation/running-tests.md", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_changed": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", "documentation/running-tests.md", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "blocking", "title": "The agent-facing reading of testament's endings still keys on exit code and error.retryable, and tells agents to retry a run that carries a real failure", "recommendation": "Class: every description of how a testament run ended that was written before `verdict` existed. Why it broke: Chunk 03 moved the runner onto testament's frozen contract and left the prose that describes the same contract on the old model. Sites found: (1) documentation/running-tests.md lines 22-24, the legend AGENTS.md sends every agent to: \"2 anything else, which is **not** a test result. Read `error.code`; when `error.retryable` is true, run again\", with no exit 75. testament's own contract (installed 0.48.0, `testament/cli.py` run help and `client.classify`) says exit 2 can be \"a test that failed before the pool cut the run short (verdict failed, a result: never retry it away)\", that such an ending is `batches_lost`, which is in `client.RETRYABLE`, and that an outage is 75. An agent following the doc reads a red run as not a result, runs it again, and can take a passing second attempt as green: exactly the defect this chunk fixed in the runner. (2) tools/ci-suite.py module docstring lines 33-35 still says outage and refusal \"are told apart by what the pool reports (`error.retryable`)\", and running-tests.md line 65 names that docstring as \"the reference for what follows\". Fix the class through one owner: make the legend relational (read `verdict`, then `verdict_reason` / `error.code`; `testament run --help` is the home for the codes, as the plan's own decision says a copy here is a second home), and change the docstring sentence to name `verdict`. Search `retryable`, `exit 2`, `exit_code` across documentation/ and tools/ for further members.", "files": ["documentation/running-tests.md", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "_why names no verdict_reason when the envelope carries no error object", "recommendation": "running-tests.md says of a refusal \"The error names it\", but `_why` falls back to \"`testament run` exited N\" when `error` is absent, so a `failed` verdict with a non-tree reason and no error object (the test fixture `(130, interrupted)`) is reported by exit code only. testament's real infra endings carry `error`, and a real exit 130 prints no envelope, so this is reachable only by envelopes testament does not emit today. Including `verdict_reason` in `_why` would close it at no cost.", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The pool job time-limit test treats DOWNLOAD_SECONDS as a bound on the download", "recommendation": "urllib's `timeout` bounds each blocking socket operation, not the whole read, and the venv/pip install has no bound, so POOL_WAIT_SECONDS + DOWNLOAD_SECONDS + 120 is not a ceiling on what the job can take. The consequence is benign: a job killed at its limit writes no `suite=` and the test job runs the whole suite. No change wanted unless the test's comment is meant as a guarantee.", "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Conventions test import block and loader", "recommendation": "`import sys` was inserted between the PyYAML comment and `import yaml`, so the comment now reads as being about `sys`; `_runner()` re-imports `importlib.util` locally with a noqa saying only these tests need it, though the module already imports it at the top; and `_runner()` duplicates `tests/test_ci_suite.py::_load`. Cosmetic.", "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": ".testament.toml's comment describes less than the runner now enforces", "recommendation": "The manifest comment (context file) says the expression \"must stay the argument after a `-m` that follows `pytest`\"; the runner now also refuses any other pytest flag after `pytest` but `-q`/`-qq`/`-v`/`-vv`/`--no-header`, and a `default_selection` other than pyproject's `testpaths`. Not false, and the refusal names the cause, so a maintainer learns it from a red job rather than the comment.", "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Acceptance criterion owed outside review: the branch's own CI run", "recommendation": "Chunk 03's criterion that the branch's CI run reports, in the `pool` job's log, that the suite ran on the pool cannot be observed by code review; confirm it on the pushed branch before merge.", "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "Records Pass and framework checks", "recommendation": "Covered files_oracle: .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md and .prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md. Both describe the runner as built (verdict keying, allowlisted selection, repo-root cwd, IncompleteRead as outage, time-limit test); the verdict values they cite match testament's `client.classify`. No bar cleared. Framework checks 7-10 do not apply: no skill, template or framework instruction file changed.", "oid": "O-6"}], "duration_seconds": 720, "scope": "ci-testament", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["03"], "chunks_proposed": ["03"], "chunk": "03", "base_reviewed": "949d39eb2e8d796b18ac4dcc5afa73f5270091a5", "record_lint": {"records": [".claude/rules/learnings/tests.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md"], "chunk_graded": "03", "chunks_graded": ["03"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": "bounded", "bounded_from": "rev-20261114T173921Z-d30347c4", "span_reason": null, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-14T17:51:25Z"}}

